  ✓  "Can I come in tomorrow at 5?" → appointment_request even without explicit service type
  ✓  "I would like to book a time for next week" → appointment.should_create=true
  ✓  "I need to schedule something" (no time given) → appointment_request — time ref not required

Suite 2: Service request classification
  ✓  "I need help with a service issue. Can someone follow up?" → service_request=true, appointment=false
  ✓  Appointment intent wins over service keyword ("schedule an appointment for a repair")
  ✓  Keyword fallback corrects OpenAI service_request misclassification → appointment_request, service_request cleared
  ✓  Appointment keyword win clears pre-existing service_request.should_create from AI, regardless of prior intent

Suite 3: General question — no record creation
  ✓  "What time are you open?" → other/general_question, no appointment, no service_request
  ✓  Front desk "service" keyword must not trigger service_request when caller says nothing actionable

Suite 4: Role mapping
  ✓  roleLabel("assistant") → "Front desk"
  ✓  roleLabel("ai") → "Front desk"
  ✓  roleLabel("agent") → "Front desk"
  ✓  roleLabel("front_desk") → "Front desk"
  ✓  roleLabel("caller") → "Caller"
  ✓  roleLabel("user") → "Caller"
  ✓  roleLabel("customer") → "Caller"
  ✓  Assistant roles never resolve to "Caller" or "You"

Suite 5: Null name/phone when caller does not provide them
  ✓  Caller who does not state name or phone → caller_name=null, caller_phone=null
  ✓  Fallback pipeline never invents caller_name or caller_phone

Suite 6: callerLinesOnly — keyword isolation
  ✓  callerLinesOnly excludes front desk lines
  ✓  Front desk "service" keyword does not trigger hasServiceKeywords after callerLinesOnly
  ✓  "appointment" in caller line triggers hasAppointmentKeywords
  ✓  "appointment" only in front desk line does not trigger hasAppointmentKeywords
  ✓  "come in" in caller line triggers hasAppointmentKeywords (no explicit "appointment" word needed)

Suite 7: Multilingual — Chinese and mixed-language
  ✓  "我想预约明天下午五点。" → appointment_request, appointment.should_create=true
  ✓  "我想 book an appointment tomorrow at 5" (mixed) → appointment_request
  ✓  "你们几点开门？" (Chinese general question) → no appointment, no service_request
  ✓  hasAppointmentKeywords matches 预约 (Chinese appointment word)

Suite 8: Semantic extraction path — non-keyword intent preservation
  ✓  "Can I come by tomorrow around five?" — model detects implicit visit+time → appointment preserved
  ✓  "Do you have time Friday afternoon?" — model detects implicit scheduling intent → appointment preserved
  ✓  "我明天下午能过去吗？" — model detects Chinese implicit visit intent → appointment preserved
  ✓  "明天五点可以吗？" — model detects Chinese time-availability query → appointment preserved
  ✓  Model appointment_request wins over service keywords present in caller text
  ✓  Pure service request (no visit intent) is preserved without upgrading to appointment
  ✓  General question (no visit/service intent) — model result produces no records

Suite 9: looksLikePhone — phone-turn detection
  ✓  phone numbers (various formats) → true
  ✓  time/date/word turns → false
  ✓  too-short / too-long digit runs → false

